{"shortDescription":"Vancouver, British Columbia--(Newsfile Corp. - October 28, 2026) - Dynasty Gold Corp. TSXV:DYG (FSE: D5G1) (OTC Oink: DGDCF) (\"Dynasty\" or the \"Company\") is pleased to report that it has received assay results from core holes drilled in its recently completed diamond drill campaign at its 100%-owne…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Vancouver, British Columbia--(Newsfile Corp. - October 28, 2026) - Dynasty Gold Corp. ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"TSXV:DYG","text":"TSXV:DYG"}}," (FSE: D5G1) (OTC Oink: DGDCF) (\"Dynasty\" or the \"Company\") is pleased to report that it has received assay results from core holes drilled in its recently completed diamond drill campaign at its 100%-owned Thundercloud project, located 200 km southeast of the gold mining hub of Red Lake and 47 km southeast of Dryden City, in the Manitou-Stormy Lakes greenstone belt of Northwest Ontario."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"This drill program extended gold mineralization vertically at both the Pelham and South-Pelham zones, confirming that the existing gold deposit(s) at Pelham continue much deeper than previously established. DP26-07 is an exciting hole, as it intersected the highest-grade mineralization at the bottom of the hole, starting from 315.5 meters; the mineralizing structure remains wide open, creating an opportunity to significantly increase the overall volume and economic value of the project. These high-grade intercepts are expected to increase tonnage and expand the baseline parameters for the next NI 43-101 resource estimate update,\" said Ivy Chong, Dynasty Gold's Chief Executive Officer and President."]},{"type":"p","children":["New mineralization was discovered by drill hole DP26-07, targeting deep extensions of the high-grade gold deposit in the Pelham Zone. This hole was designed to test down-plunge mineralization towards the eastern end; it has successfully extended the known footprint to 323 meters at depth at the Pelham Zone. Hole DP26-07 intersected high gold values near the bottom of the hole; five consecutive samples taken between 315.5 meters and 323 meters returned gold values up to 6.26 grams per ton (g/t) (",{"type":"b","children":["Table 1"]},"). The deposit remains open, both along strike and at depth (",{"type":"b","children":["Figure 1"]},"). DP26-06 also tested down-dip mineralization within the zone; only partial results have been received. Assays from Holes 6, 8 to 14 will be released when available."]},{"type":"news-image","params":{"image":{"id":"tmx_newsfile:c5ab60cbe094b-eeeaa439e98214b342e0dad9422b1b02","source-width":1171,"source-height":516,"bg-color":"#7d756a"}}},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Figure 1: Pelham Deposit Looking West"]}]},{"type":"p","children":["To view an enhanced version of this graphic, please visit:"]},{"type":"news-image","params":{"image":{"id":"tmx_newsfile:c5ab60cbe094b-eeeaa439e98214b342e0dad9422b1b02","source-width":1171,"source-height":516,"bg-color":"#7d756a"}}},{"type":"p","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Table 1: Pelham Drill Intercepts Highlights"]}]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Hole Number"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Targets"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Zone"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["From (m)"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["To "]},{"type":"b","children":["(m)"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Interval (m)"]}]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"b","children":["Au "]},{"type":"b","children":["(g/t)"]}]}]},{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["DP26-07"]},{"type":"table-data-cell","children":["Testing Down-Plunge extension"]},{"type":"ta